title: select-for-update prim landed; storage.transactions remains partial pending opt-in weaker-isolation query-isolation passthrough
severity: low
status: resolved
section: storage.transactions
reporter: agent (iteration 17, 2026-07-06)

summary:
  The (select-for-update 'type id) primitive, referenced in
  [storage.transactions] doc text ("Explicit row locks:
   (select-for-update 'type id) Exposed as a primitive for finer
  control"), is now genuinely IMPLEMENTED as of it17 (2026-07-06).

  Implementation:
    - image/lib/crud.ml: Crud.select_for_update — executes
      `SELECT fields::text FROM data_rows WHERE type_name=$1 AND
      id=$2::uuid FOR UPDATE`. Returns the locked row's fields JSON
      as a VStr, or VNil if no row.
    - image/lib/session.ml: register_crud_prims extended with the
      `select-for-update` prim.

  Smoke test preserved at /tmp/pp_sfu_it17.py — verifies:
    - real PG SELECT ... FOR UPDATE returns the row's fields JSON
    - composition (dict-get (select-for-update ...)) works
    - arity-error path returns a graceful VStr, no REPL crash

  CAVEAT — transactional scope:
    The PG-side SELECT ... FOR UPDATE lock is only useful inside a
    surrounding transaction. v1's Lisp API has no
    (with-transaction ...) prim yet — pgx wraps each statement in an
    implicit transaction, so the lock is released as soon as the
    statement returns. The "REAL" use of this prim awaits a future
    (with-transaction ...) prim that wraps a bodyOfWork in
    Store.with_transaction so the FOR UPDATE lock holds for the
    duration. The prim is still useful AS A HINT today, but its
    concurrency-protection semantics are inert outside a real tx.

  STORAGE.TRANSACTIONS STATUS REMAINS PARTIAL:
    The OTHER unbuilt sub-feature of [storage.transactions] is the
    "opt-in weaker isolation: (query ... isolation: 'read-committed)
    Available but discouraged". This isn't yet built either — the
    (query ...) form doesn't exist. The Query_prim would need to
    take an optional isolation argument and pass it to
    Store.with_transaction's ?isolation parameter. No spec change
    needed — just implementation work for a future iteration.

    Section should remain `partial` until BOTH sub-features (the
    opt-in weaker-isolation query passthrough AND a
    (with-transaction ...) prim that makes select-for-update
    transactionally meaningful) are present. Or split the section:
      (subsection serializable-by-default) = implemented (today's reality)
      (subsection explicit-locks)         = implemented as of it17
      (subsection opt-in-weaker-isolation) = planned
    A future plan-mode pass should resolve this — see BORGE-1783433175
    and BORGE-1783435057 for the broader plan-pass request tracking
    storage.* and the multi-section status transition map.

verified-at-iteration:
  17 (2026-07-06)
  - dune build @all exit 0
  - dune runtest --force 92 tests pass (no regressions)
  - /tmp/pp_sfu_it17.py PASSES (4 assertions: create returns UUID,
    select-for-update returns fields JSON, dict-get composes on the
    locked row, bad-args returns graceful error)
  - prior dev-stack smoke tests re-verified green: pp_e2e_it6,
    pp_fork_it9, pp_merge_it10, pp_checkout_it11, pp_crud_it13.

